# Lumenhold Academy — 简体中文 (zh-CN) translation of content/endings.grim
# Maintained by `node tools/grim.js i18n zh-CN`. Translate the text after "="; keep {tokens}.
# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@ending ending_sent_home
# en: Sent Home
title [a6af26] = 被送回家
# en: The infirmary writes to your family. A carriage comes for you on a grey morning and you watch the towers shrink in the rear window. Your body gave out before your dreams did. Perhaps, one day, you will come back.
text [9741e7] = 医务室给你家里写了信。一个灰蒙蒙的早晨，马车来接你，你从后窗看着高塔渐渐缩小。你的身体先于你的梦想垮掉了。也许有一天，你还会回来。

@ending ending_quiet_departure
# en: The Quiet Departure
title [b17cb0] = 悄然离去
# en: You take the dawn barge without telling anyone. The academy does not notice right away; then, one by one, people do. Some of them write. You keep the letters in a box you don't open for years. When you finally do, you are someone gentler, and you find you are not alone.
text [e6ed08] = 你没告诉任何人，搭上了黎明的驳船。学院起初并没察觉；后来，人们一个接一个地发现了。有些人给你写了信。你把信收进一只盒子，好多年都没打开。等你终于打开时，你已变得更温柔，而且发现自己并不孤单。

@ending ending_expelled
# en: Expelled
title [a01536] = 开除学籍
# en: The Board's decision is final. Your wand is not taken — Lumenhold is not cruel — but your name is struck from the register in ink that cannot be unwritten. You walk out of the gates with a trunk and a lesson, and the long road ahead is entirely your own.
text [27607d] = 委员会的决定无法更改。你的魔杖没有被收走——流明堡并不残忍——但你的名字被一种无法抹去的墨水从名册上划掉了。你提着行李箱、带着一个教训走出校门，前方的漫漫长路，完全属于你自己。

@ending ending_hollow_claimed
# en: Claimed by the Hollow Star
title [83514d] = 被空洞之星吞噬
# en: You open the door beneath the lake. The Hollow Star looks back. For a moment you understand everything, and then there is no "you" left to understand it. On clear nights students swear they see a new star, black against black, right above the seventh tower.
text [205ca2] = 你打开了湖底之门。空洞之星回望着你。有那么一瞬间，你明白了一切；随后，再也没有一个“你”能去明白什么了。晴朗的夜里，学生们发誓看见了一颗新星——黑上之黑——就在第七塔的正上方。

@ending ending_runaway
# en: Gone With the Wind
title [d9dde5] = 随风而去
# en: You and Corvin leave Lumenhold on a stolen sky-barge at midnight, laughing so hard you can barely steer. The academy will tell the story for years — usually wrong. You never graduate. You don't regret it, mostly.
text [c5d68b] = 午夜时分，你和科尔文驾着一艘偷来的天空驳船离开了流明堡，笑得几乎掌不稳舵。学院会把这个故事讲上好多年——而且通常讲错。你始终没有毕业。你并不后悔，大体上。

@ending ending_hollow_keeper
# en: Keeper of the Hollow Star
title [3ac5e6] = 空洞之星的守护者
# en: You graduate with a black star on your palm and a voice in the back of your mind that is not entirely yours. The Hollow Star gave you power; it will want something back. For now, the towers bow a little when you pass, and even the headmistress looks away first.
text [8bdf91] = 你毕业时，掌心带着一颗黑色的星，脑海深处还有一个不完全属于你的声音。空洞之星给了你力量；它总有一天会要回些什么。至于现在，你经过时高塔都会微微低头，连院长都会先移开目光。

@ending ending_hollow_freed
# en: Herald of the Hollow Star
title [5e0dc6] = 空洞之星的使者
# en: The spring the lake froze, the Star went free, and you held the door. It did not swallow you; it remembered who let it out. The Northern families write to you as one of their own now, and wherever you walk, candles burn a little lower, as if bowing. Lumenhold still hands you a diploma. Nobody at the ceremony looks you in the eye.
text [0ea418] = 湖面冰封的那个春天，星挣脱而去，而为它扶住门的是你。它没有吞掉你；它记得是谁放它出来的。如今北境的世家把你当作自家人来写信，你走到哪里，烛火便低下去一点，像在鞠躬。流明堡照样发给你毕业证书。典礼上没有一个人敢直视你的眼睛。

@ending ending_hollow_failed
# en: The Night Was Lost
title [3fa69b] = 失落之夜
# en: The spring the lake froze, you went down beneath it, and the door would not close for you. The headmistress closed it in your place and paid for it with years she didn't have to spare. The Wardens don't blame you. Every spring, when the lake thaws, you do, a little, and then you get up and keep the old doors anyway.
text [41dc15] = 湖面封冻的那个春天，你下到了湖底，而那扇门不肯为你合上。校长替你关上了它，付出的是她本已所剩无多的岁月。守望者们不怪你。每年春天湖水解冻时，你会怪自己一点点，然后起身，照旧守着那些古老的门。

@ending ending_hollow_hero
# en: Warden of Lumenhold
title [1eb489] = 流明堡的守望者
# en: The academy will never fully know what you did beneath the lake. The headmistress does. At graduation she gives you a silver key without a lock and a seat among the Wardens, the quiet few who keep the old doors closed. Kael stands in the crowd and, for once, he is smiling.
text [fff990] = 学院永远不会完全知道你在湖底做了什么。院长知道。毕业典礼上，她交给你一把没有锁的银钥匙，以及守望者中的一席之地——那是守护古老之门、默默无闻的少数人。凯尔站在人群里，难得地，他在微笑。

@ending ending_archmage
# en: The Archmage's Path
title [fea2fb] = 大法师之路
# en: In the autumn you climb the steps of the Seven Towers in a new grey robe, an apprentice of the Conclave, with seven years of wards and failures ahead and a desk that faces a wall of locked books. Professor Thorne shakes your hand at the gate and says, gruffly, "Don't waste it." You won't.
text [a36d7c] = 秋天，你穿着崭新的灰袍登上七塔的台阶，成为七塔议会的学徒。前面是七年的护界与失败，还有一张对着一整面上锁书墙的书桌。索恩教授在门口和你握手，粗声说：“别浪费了。”你不会的。

@ending ending_scholar
# en: Scholar of the Spire
title [02e34a] = 尖塔学者
# en: Your thesis is shelved in the Spire Library, in the section students whisper about, and you take the junior fellowship that came with it. You will spend your life among books that bite and secrets that wait — and you could not be happier.
text [5472ac] = 你的毕业论文被收进尖塔图书馆，放在学生们低声谈论的那一区；随它而来的初级研究员职位，你也接下了。你将在会咬人的书和静静等待的秘密之间度过一生——而你再快乐不过。

@ending ending_beloved
# en: Hand in Hand
title [b32cc8] = 携手同行
# en: Graduation is a blur of robes and cheers, but what you remember is a hand finding yours as the hats go up. Whatever comes next, you won't face it alone. Lumenhold taught you magic; it also taught you this.
text [ad5713] = 毕业典礼是长袍与欢呼交织的一片模糊，但你记得的，是帽子抛向空中时，一只手找到了你的手。无论接下来是什么，你都不会独自面对。流明堡教会了你魔法；也教会了你这个。

@ending ending_beloved_lyra
# en: The Second Flame
title [c90153] = 第二簇火焰
# en: When the hats go up, {lyra} catches yours before it lands and hands it back without a word. Later, in front of her whole family, she takes your hand and doesn't let go. For House Vaneshade, that is a declaration. For her it is simpler: she has finally found someone she doesn't need to beat.
text [1b430a] = 帽子抛向天空时，{lyra} 在你的帽子落地前接住了它，一言不发地递还给你。之后，当着她全家人的面，她握住你的手，再也没有松开。对凡妮希德家族来说，这是一份宣言；对她来说，事情更简单：她终于找到了一个不必去赢的人。

@ending ending_beloved_tobias
# en: Home, Wherever
title [4a14ae] = 无论何处皆是家
# en: {tobias} cries through the whole ceremony and blames the pollen. Afterwards he lifts you off your feet in front of everyone, then shows you a drawing of a farmhouse with two chairs on the porch. "No pressure," he says. "The goats have already voted."
text [f06768] = {tobias} 哭完了整场典礼，坚称是花粉过敏。之后他当着所有人的面把你抱离地面，又给你看一张画：一座农舍，门廊上摆着两把椅子。“不着急，”他说，“山羊们已经投过票了。”

@ending ending_beloved_seraphine
# en: Already Foreseen
title [350c84] = 早已预见
# en: "I saw this," {seraphine} says as the hats go up. "Years ago. You were holding my hand." You are. For once she smiles at the present, as if it has finally caught up with her, and asks whether you'd like to know what happens next. You tell her you'd rather find out together.
text [c966c4] = “我见过这一幕，”帽子抛起时 {seraphine} 说，“好几年前。你握着我的手。”你确实握着。她难得地对着此刻微笑，仿佛现在终于追上了她，然后问你想不想知道接下来会发生什么。你说你宁愿和她一起去发现。

@ending ending_beloved_corvin
# en: No More Jokes
title [ffc267] = 不再说笑
# en: {corvin} slips a key into your palm during the speeches. It opens nothing at Lumenhold; he has checked. "It's for wherever we end up," he says, and for once he doesn't make a joke of it. Then he does, of course. But his hand stays in yours.
text [83042c] = 致辞的时候，{corvin} 把一把钥匙塞进你掌心。它在流明堡打不开任何一扇门——他检查过了。“这是给我们将来落脚的地方用的，”他说，难得没有拿它开玩笑。当然，过了一会儿他还是开了个玩笑。但他的手一直握着你的。

@ending ending_beloved_mir
# en: Built to Last
title [66dc88] = 经久耐用
# en: {mir} has rigged the hats to fly back down. Most of them do. In the cheerful chaos they press a small brass ring into your hand; it ticks faintly, like a second heart. "It'll run for fifty years," they say. "Probably. We should check."
text [36f87a] = {mir} 给帽子装了机关，让它们自己飞回来。大部分确实飞回来了。在一片欢乐的混乱里，TA 把一枚小小的黄铜戒指按进你手心：它轻轻地滴答作响，像第二颗心脏。“能走五十年，”TA 说，“大概吧。我们得一起验证一下。”

@ending ending_beloved_kael
# en: Thaw
title [448405] = 解冻
# en: {kael} doesn't throw his hat. He stands beside you in the crowd, and when the cheering is loudest he says, very quietly, "Come north with me. Or I stay. Either." It is the longest sentence about feelings he has ever spoken. His hand, in yours, is warm.
text [edf40c] = {kael} 没有抛帽子。他站在人群里你的身边，在欢呼声最响的时候，非常轻地说：“跟我去北方吧。或者我留下。都行。”这是他说过的最长的一句关于感情的话。他握在你手里的手，是温暖的。

@ending ending_beloved_nessa
# en: Front Page
title [c50df3] = 头版
# en: The Ledger's graduation issue runs a small notice at the bottom of page six, set in {nessa}'s own type: two names, one line, no comment. All of Lumenhold reads it before breakfast. {nessa} pretends not to watch them read it, and holds your hand under the table the whole time.
text [ed9fec] = 《流明纪事报》的毕业特刊在第六版底部登了一则小启事，用的是 {nessa} 自己的铅字：两个名字，一行字，不加评论。全流明堡的人都在早饭前读到了它。{nessa} 假装没在看大家读它，却在桌子底下一直握着你的手。

@ending ending_alchemist
# en: Master of the Crucible
title [cd1134] = 坩埚大师
# en: Your potions are already sold under the counter in three cities. On graduation day you sign the lease on the crooked little shop by the harbour. The sign reads your name, and underneath: NO REFUNDS FOR TRANSFORMATIONS.
text [133fe4] = 你的药剂早已在三座城市的柜台底下卖开了。毕业那天，你签下了港口边那间歪歪扭扭的小铺子的租约。招牌上写着你的名字，下面一行：变形概不退款。

@ending ending_celebrity
# en: The Name on Every Lip
title [264e3e] = 人人口中的名字
# en: The Lumen Ledger runs a special edition about you. First-years queue for your autograph. You graduate as the most talked-about student in a generation, and the world beyond the gates is already waiting to hear what you'll do next.
text [208c47] = 《流明纪事报》为你出了一期特刊。一年级新生排队找你签名。你作为一代人中最受热议的学生毕业，而校门外的世界，早已等着听你接下来要做什么。

@ending ending_merchant
# en: Gold in the Vaults
title [2332ee] = 金库满盈
# en: You leave Lumenhold with a diploma, a fortune and an old partner's desk in a harbour shipping house. Magic, you've decided, is good, but compound interest is better. Within five years the house has offices in every port — and an enchanted ledger that never loses a coin.
text [a52912] = 你离开流明堡时，带着一张文凭、一笔财富，和港口一家航运商行里一位老合伙人的书桌。你认定魔法固然好，复利更好。不出五年，商行在每座港口都有了办事处——还有一本从不丢一枚硬币的附魔账簿。

@ending ending_shadow
# en: The Quiet Hand
title [9eb5a5] = 无声之手
# en: No one quite knows how you graduated with those grades. No one quite remembers the favours you called in. In the autumn you take a desk at the Crown's Office of Unseen Affairs, in a building with no sign and no address. You'd found it, of course, long before they told you where it was.
text [930717] = 没人说得清你是怎么凭那样的成绩毕业的，也没人记得你讨回了哪些人情。秋天，你在王室隐秘事务署有了一张书桌，那栋楼没有招牌，也没有地址。当然，早在他们告诉你之前，你就已经找到了它。

@ending ending_beloved_friends
# en: The Ones Who Stayed
title [5337c3] = 留下来的人
# en: You may not leave as the brightest or the richest, but you leave surrounded. Your friends throw their hats higher than anyone's, and the photograph from that day — all of you squinting into the sun — will hang in every home you ever have.
text [8d3051] = 你离开时也许不是最聪明的，也不是最富有的，但你被大家簇拥着。你的朋友们把帽子抛得比谁都高；那天的合影——大家都在阳光里眯着眼——会挂在你今后住过的每一个家里。

@ending ending_barely
# en: By the Skin of Your Teeth
title [434e96] = 惊险过关
# en: Your name is called last, after a long pause and some whispering between examiners. But it is called. You graduate. You are a mage of Lumenhold, and nobody ever has to know the details.
text [7c93a5] = 在一段长长的停顿和考官之间的窃窃私语之后，你的名字最后一个被念到。但终究被念到了。你毕业了。你是流明堡的法师，没人需要知道其中的细节。

@ending ending_bystander
# en: Someone Else's Lantern
title [93af7a] = 别人的灯笼
# en: There was a spring frost, the year you graduated, and a night when the bell under the lake would not stop ringing. You were somewhere else: asleep, or studying, or holding a door shut for the first-years. Someone else went down with the lantern. You never learn their whole story, but every spring, when the lake thaws, you find yourself grateful to them.
text [737b03] = 你毕业那年下过一场春霜，还有一个夜晚，湖底的钟响个不停。那时你在别处：在睡觉，在读书，或是替一年级生死死顶住一扇门。提着灯笼下去的是别人。你始终没能知道他们的全部故事，但每年春天湖水解冻时，你总会发现自己在心里默默感谢他们。

@ending ending_graduate
# en: A Mage of Lumenhold
title [691b6b] = 流明堡的法师
# en: Robes, hats, a speech that runs long. You walk out of the gates of Lumenhold a qualified mage — not legendary, not disgraced, simply yourself, with four years of stories and a whole world to spend them in.
text [7b1e39] = 长袍、学位帽，一场拖得太长的致辞。你作为一名合格的法师走出流明堡的大门——不算传奇，也不丢人，只是你自己，带着四年的故事，和一整个可以挥霍它们的世界。

@ending ending_teacher
# en: The Teacher's Desk
title [b21115] = 讲台之后
# en: In the autumn you return to Lumenhold — not on the student barge, but on the faculty one. Your classroom has a window over the lake and a desk with somebody else's initials carved in it. On the first day a terrified first-year asks a question you once asked. You know exactly what to say.
text [dce2bc] = 秋天，你回到了流明堡——不是坐学生的驳船，而是坐教职员的那一艘。你的教室有一扇面朝湖水的窗，讲桌上刻着别人的名字缩写。开学第一天，一个吓坏了的一年级生问了一个你当年也问过的问题。你完全知道该怎么回答。

@ending ending_wanderer
# en: The Road of Wonders
title [055eab] = 奇迹之路
# en: You join the Travelling Circus of Wonders as its youngest illusionist. For years you cross the kingdoms in a painted wagon, making dragons out of moonlight for children who have never seen magic. Every winter, a letter arrives from Lumenhold. You always write back.
text [31dcb2] = 你加入了奇迹巡回马戏团，成了团里最年轻的幻术师。多年来，你坐着彩绘马车穿越一个又一个王国，用月光为从未见过魔法的孩子们变出巨龙。每年冬天，都会有一封来自流明堡的信。你每一封都回。

@ending ending_tamsin_friends
# en: A Friend Across the Hills
title [c7176e] = 山那边的朋友
# en: Your yearbook entry has a green seal pressed into the corner, which is not allowed. Tamsin Reed of Thornwick sent it, with a note: "Four years of rivalry, four hundred letters, one friend. Insufferable to the end." Every spring, at a town halfway between, there are biscuits.
text [fb273b] = 你的毕业纪念册角落里压着一枚绿色的封蜡，这是不允许的。是荆木学院的塔姆辛·里德寄来的，附了张字条：“四年的较劲，四百封信，一个朋友。到最后都让人受不了。”每年春天，在两校中间的一座小镇上，都有饼干。

@ending ending_dumonts_reunited
# en: Two Dumonts in the Photograph
title [51d393] = 合影里的两个杜蒙
# en: In the graduation photograph, at the edge of the crowd, two pale heads lean together: Kael, and the sister who was raised to open the door he refused. Neither of them is smiling at the camera. They are smiling at each other, which is rarer, and which you helped to happen.
text [d79ff1] = 毕业合影里，人群边上，两颗浅色的脑袋靠在一起：凯尔，和那个被养大来打开他拒绝打开的那扇门的妹妹。他们谁都没有对着镜头笑。他们是在对彼此笑——这更难得，而你帮了这个忙。

@ending ending_ilse_taken
# en: A Chair Left Empty
title [c33d8b] = 一把空着的椅子
# en: The man in grey took Ilse north, and no letter has come. At graduation Kael keeps the seat beside him empty without saying why. You know why. Some evenings, when the lake goes very still, you still look for a girl in white furs on the far shore.
text [9df500] = 灰衣人把伊尔泽带去了北境，至今没有一封信。毕业典礼上，凯尔身旁的座位一直空着，他没说为什么。你知道为什么。有些傍晚，湖面静得出奇的时候，你仍会在对岸寻找一个穿白裘的女孩。

@ending ending_thesis_hollowstar
# en: The Thesis They Locked Away
title [dad732] = 被锁起来的论文
# en: Your thesis on the founders' seal earned a distinction and then disappeared into the headmistress's tower. Its catalogue card in the Spire Library reads only "Restricted", in her handwriting. Three people in the world have read it. One of them still writes to you with questions.
text [b15104] = 你关于创始者封印的毕业论文拿到了优等，随后便消失在院长塔里。尖塔图书馆里它的目录卡上只写着"禁阅"二字，是她的笔迹。世上读过它的只有三个人，其中一个至今还写信来向你请教。

@ending ending_lumen
# en: A Lantern for Others
title [217ba6] = 为他人提灯的人
# en: In the yearbook, under your portrait, someone has written: "The one you went to when it mattered." First-years you barely remember will name their own lanterns after you. Lumenhold has a word for people like that. It is the same word as its name.
text [2de9cf] = 年鉴上，你的肖像下面有人写了一句：“要紧的时候，大家去找的那个人。”你几乎记不得的一年级生，日后会用你的名字给自己的灯笼命名。流明堡对这样的人有个说法——就是它自己的名字。

@ending ending_hollow_touched
# en: The Shadow at Your Heel
title [b9eb7a] = 跟在脚边的影子
# en: Your portrait in the yearbook is the only one where the candles behind you seem to have gone out. People step aside when you pass, not quite knowing why. The Hollow has learned your name, and you find, more and more often, that you answer to it.
text [7dd587] = 整本年鉴里，只有你的肖像身后的烛火像是熄了。人们在你经过时让开路，却说不清为什么。空洞已经知道了你的名字，而你越来越常发现，自己会应声。

@ending ending_hollow_fled
# en: The Door Left Ajar
title [8b2193] = 虚掩的门
# en: You went down beneath the frozen lake, saw the door, and ran. Nobody blames you to your face; the headmistress, whose hair went white that night, never mentions it at all. Somewhere under the water the door still stands ajar. Every spring, when the ice goes out, you dream of the dark between the gap and the frame.
text [7942e9] = 你下到冰封的湖底，看见了那扇门，然后逃了。没人当面责怪你；院长的头发在那一夜白了，她从此只字不提。在水下某处，那扇门仍然虚掩着。每年春天冰融的时候，你都会梦见门缝与门框之间的那片黑暗。

@ending ending_held_the_line
# en: The Night Above the Ice
title [f8ba13] = 冰面之上的夜
# en: The night the lake froze, you didn't go down. You held the doors of the first-year tower against frost and whispers until dawn, and every child in it lived. Someone else went beneath the lake, or no one did; the first-years never cared which. They carved your initials over that door, and nobody has dared paint them out.
text [b536e5] = 湖面冰封的那一夜，你没有下去。你守住一年级塔楼的门，抵挡寒霜与低语，一直到天亮，楼里的每个孩子都活了下来。有人下到了湖底，又或者谁也没有；一年级生们从不在意是哪种。他们把你名字的缩写刻在那扇门上方，没人敢把它涂掉。

@ending ending_royal_archivist
# en: Keeper of the Folios
title [17c7cf] = 对开本的守护人
# en: You take the cold room at the Royal Library Archives, the one with the folios that object to being opened. Within a year you have catalogued a shelf nobody had dared touch in a century, and the keeper has stopped checking your gloves. On the staff list, under "Cataloguer", your name is in copperplate.
text [60f61d] = 你接下了皇家图书馆档案馆那间冷房间，里面的对开本都不愿被翻开。不到一年，你就编好了一整架百年来没人敢碰的书，馆长也不再检查你的手套。员工名册的“编目员”一栏下，你的名字用铜版体写着。

@ending ending_guild
# en: A Bench at the Works
title [e6bbfa] = 工坊里的一张工作台
# en: You join the Guild of Alchemists' great works as its newest journeyman, in protective clothing you paid for yourself. There are two explosions a month and none of them yours. By the second winter the foreman sends the hardest batches to your bench, and pretends he doesn't.
text [60508c] = 你作为最新的熟练工加入了炼金师公会的大工坊，穿着自己花钱买的防护服。那里每月炸两次，没有一次是你。到第二个冬天，工头把最难的那批料都送到你的工作台，还装作没这回事。

@ending ending_observatory
# en: Charting the Night
title [3efc38] = 绘制夜空
# en: You go back up to the plateau with the Observatory Expedition, salaried now, frostbite remedies in your pack. The nights are long and very cold and you stay awake through every one of them. Two years on, a star on the new charts carries your initials, in very small letters.
text [a7f87f] = 你随观星远征回到高原，这次领着薪水，背包里装着冻疮药。夜晚漫长而寒冷，你每一夜都醒着熬到天亮。两年后，新星图上有一颗星标着你名字的缩写，字写得很小很小。

@ending ending_field_station
# en: Out on the Moors
title [6c6ba9] = 荒原之上
# en: You take the keeper's cottage at the Beastcraft Field Station: a lamp, a kettle, and more creatures than any sane person would count. The winters are long, wet and lonely. You count the creatures anyway, every one, and the foal from your summer grows up following you about like a dog.
text [651754] = 你住进了驭兽术野外站的看守小屋：一盏灯、一把水壶，还有正常人根本数不过来的生灵。冬天又长又湿又孤单。你还是把它们一只只数过来，而你那个夏天的小马驹长大了，像小狗一样跟着你转。

@ending ending_thornwick
# en: Across the Hills
title [d009b3] = 翻过山去
# en: You cross the hills to Thornwick's illusion laboratory, where they think glamour is a science and are mostly right. Lumenhold says something cutting about it, as predicted. Within three years it offers to hire you back at twice the salary, as predicted. You haven't answered yet.
text [9bb7da] = 你翻过山，去了荆木学院的幻术实验室，那里的人认为魅影是一门科学，而且大多是对的。流明堡对此说了些尖刻的话，正如所料。不到三年，它又开出双倍的薪水想把你请回来，也正如所料。你还没回信。

@ending ending_librarian
# en: The Stacks Kept You
title [06374c] = 书库留下了你
# en: You never quite leave. In the autumn you are back behind the Spire Library's reference desk, a keeper of the stacks now, with a longer ladder and a key to the shelves nobody else may reach. Footnote has not bitten you in months. Students ask you for books, and you find them every time.
text [5a506b] = 你从没真正离开。秋天，你又回到尖塔图书馆的咨询台后，如今是书库的看守人，有了一架更长的梯子，和一把别人够不着的书架的钥匙。脚注已经好几个月没咬过你了。学生们来找书，你每次都能找到。

@ending ending_newt
# en: Behind the Bar
title [7962ab] = 吧台后面
# en: You stay on at the Gilded Newt, full time, behind the bar and then in charge of it. You remember who ordered the spiced cider, and who's owed a favour, and which of the card games upstairs to look away from. Students who were first-years when you graduated come in to tell you their troubles. You pour, and listen.
text [cc89de] = 你留在了镀金蝾螈酒馆，全职，先是站吧台，后来管整个店。你记得谁点了香料苹果酒，谁欠着人情，楼上哪桌牌局该当没看见。你毕业时还是一年级的学生，如今也会来跟你倒苦水。你倒酒，然后听。

@ending ending_pell
# en: Counting Drops
title [77984e] = 数着药滴
# en: You stay on at Pell & Daughters, at the counter by day and among the thousand drawers by night, counting drops while Old Pell counts aloud behind you. In ten years, if you're still careful, they'll show you the drawers that never open. You are still careful.
text [e4d757] = 你留在了佩尔父女药铺，白天守柜台，夜里在上千个抽屉之间，数着药滴，老佩尔在你身后大声数着。十年后，如果你还够仔细，他们会让你看那些从不打开的抽屉。你一直很仔细。

@ending ending_courier
# en: Over the Lake in All Weathers
title [08a192] = 风雨无阻飞越湖面
# en: You keep the satchel with your name on the flap and fly the lake in all weathers, letters and parcels and the occasional live delivery. The broom still pulls left. You don't. On winter nights the first-years watch your lamp crossing the ice and make wishes on it, as if you were a star.
text [e98015] = 你留着那个翻盖上绣着你名字的挎包，风雨无阻地飞越湖面，送信件、包裹，偶尔还有活物。扫帚还是往左偏，你不会。冬夜里，一年级生们看着你的灯越过冰面，对它许愿，仿佛你是一颗星。

@ending ending_clerk
# en: A Desk and a Stamp
title [4ec5f0] = 一张书桌和一枚印章
# en: You take the clerk's desk from the registrar's list: stamps, ledgers and a window that looks at a wall. It isn't a dream. It pays the rent, and in the evenings you are free, and one day, quietly, you notice that the wall has a crack in it shaped exactly like a door.
text [32fd73] = 你接下了教务员清单上那张书记员的桌子：印章、账簿，还有一扇对着墙的窗。这不是梦想。它付得起房租，晚上你是自由的；有一天，你悄悄发现那面墙上有一道裂缝，形状恰好像一扇门。

@ending ending_still_searching
# en: Still Looking
title [4c93f8] = 还在寻找
# en: You graduate without a post, and on purpose, or near enough. Your grades will open doors and your name has been heard; the world, you've decided, can make you a better offer in its own time. You spend the autumn writing letters from a rented room above a bakery. Some of them get answers.
text [db163a] = 你没有带着职位毕业，而且几乎是故意的。你的成绩会打开门，你的名字也有人听说过；你认定这个世界可以在它自己的时候给你开个更好的价。整个秋天，你在面包房楼上租来的房间里写信。有一些得到了回音。

@ending ending_back_home
# en: Back in Your Old Room
title [800d40] = 回到你的旧房间
# en: You go home with a diploma and no letter. Your old room is smaller than you remember, and the bed is too short, and for a while you lie in it until noon and let the days rot quietly by. Then, one morning, you sit up, and write to the registrar about her list. It was still there, as she said it would be.
text [3d707b] = 你带着一张文凭、没有一封聘书回了家。旧房间比你记忆里小，床也太短；有一阵子，你躺在上面睡到中午，任日子悄悄烂掉。后来某个早晨，你坐起身，给教务员写信，问起她那张清单。它还在那儿，就像她说过的那样。
